+**Claim, stated precisely.** lccc identifies as GCC 16.2.0, answers the driver
+queries identically, defines the same macro set where the spelling is
+immaterial, agrees on the five default-error diagnostics, and answers
+`__has_builtin`/`__has_attribute`/`__has_feature` **truthfully** — it never
+claims a builtin, attribute or feature it does not implement. It implements
+123 of GCC 16.2's 161 probe-visible builtins and 79 of its 81 attributes, and
+the 38 + 2 + 3 gaps are enumerated with ids in the gate. That is the bounded
+claim; the unbounded one ("compatible with GCC 16.2") is not made here.
