+## 15. Round 3 — closing the gaps the gate exposed
+
+Section 14 left four `KNOWN_OPEN` tables. This section removes entries from
+them by implementing the feature, and shrinks the rest, with the evidence for
+each. Nothing below is a claim: every item names the oracle-comparison that
+proves it.
+
+### 15.1 Implemented in this round
+
+| Feature | Evidence |
+|---|---|
+| `__TIMESTAMP__` | byte-identical to gcc-16.2.0 for a file with a pinned mtime (`touch -d '2020-01-02 03:04:05'`) -> `"Thu Jan  2 03:04:05 2020"`. `asctime` rendering (space-padded day) and local-time conversion; `"???"` when the file cannot be `stat`ed |
+| `__FILE_NAME__` | matches for `#include`-nested files: `"a.h"` while `__FILE__` is `"sub/a.h"`; follows `#line` like `__FILE__` |
+| `__INCLUDE_LEVEL__` | 0 in the main file, 1/2 through nested `#include`s, restoring on pop |
+| `_Maxof` / `_Minof` (GCC 15/16) | new `Expr::TypeLimit` AST node threaded through parser, sema, constant folder and lowering. Identical values on a 12-row matrix (`int`, `unsigned`, `long long`, `_Bool`, `char`, `unsigned char`, `short`, `unsigned short`, enum with/without negatives, typedef, `__int128`), valid in every constant context (static initialiser, file-scope array bound, `case` label, `_Static_assert`), and the five documented error forms reject with GCC's wording ("invalid application of '_Maxof' to type 'double'") |
+| 14 `__builtin_stdc_*` (C23 `<stdbit.h>`) | **923,079 value cases** against the oracle: *every* 8-bit and 16-bit input, all 14 functions, plus edge set + random sample for 32/64-bit, plus a `_Generic` result-type matrix and a single-evaluation probe. `tests/regression/check_stdbit_builtins.py` |
+| 8 `__builtin_{huge_val,inf,nan,nans}f{32,64}` | values and result types match; `_Float32`/`_Float64` are `float`/`double` here by construction |
+| Character constants in `#if` | multichar packing, 5-byte truncation, single-character sign extension, hex/octal/simple escapes, UCN -> UTF-8 all match (`tests/regression/check_char_and_dynamic_macros.py`) |
+| Quoted `#include` search order | an extra fallback to the *main* file's directory was removed (`check_quoted_include_search.py`) |
+
+### 15.2 Two defects found *by* the work, and what they taught
+
+1. **`__attribute__((aligned))` with no argument was a silent no-op.**  A
+   `struct __attribute__((aligned)) s { char c; };` is 16 bytes to every
+   GCC-compiled object and was **1** here — an ABI defect, not a missing
+   warning. Fixed with `target_biggest_alignment()`; the new gate compares
+   layouts *and* `offsetof`, and pins 16/32/64 for `-mavx`/`-mavx512f`.
+2. **A quoted include could reach out of the including file's directory.**
+   With `sub/t.c -> sub/deep/b.h -> "a.h"`, lccc pulled in `sub/a.h` where GCC
+   (correctly) fails. Compiling against the *wrong header* is worse than
+   failing, so the fallback is gone.
+
+### 15.3 What is still open, and precisely why
+
+The `KNOWN_OPEN_*` tables in `tests/regression/check_gcc16_compat.py` are the
+authority; this is the summary. Each remaining entry names the blocker, not a
+preference.
+
+| id | item | blocker |
+|----|------|---------|
